# Line endings, pinned.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF in the working
# tree. Biome formats with LF and has no CRLF-tolerant mode, so a file that git
# converted on checkout fails `biome check` on the developer's machine while
# passing in CI, which checks out on Linux. The symptom is a formatting error on
# a file nobody touched.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for this repository, so the working tree matches
# what is stored and what CI sees. Repository content is already LF throughout,
# so no renormalisation is needed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to translate anything inside them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Kept out of diffs so a lockfile change does not bury a review.
bun.lock linguist-generated=true
lib/database.types.ts linguist-generated=true
